        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^3+3x^2+5)^4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12(x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(x^3+3x^2+5)^4&=4(x^3+3x^2+5)^3(3x^2+6x)\\\\&=12(x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int 12(x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x^3+3x^2+5)^4+C$",
          "worked": "From part a, the integrand is the derivative of $(x^3+3x^2+5)^4$.\n$$\\int 12(x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\,dx=(x^3+3x^2+5)^4+C$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int (x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{12}(x^3+3x^2+5)^4+C$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\int (x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\,dx&=\\frac{1}{12}\\int 12(x^2+2x)(x^3+3x^2+5)^3\\,dx\\\\&=\\frac{1}{12}(x^3+3x^2+5)^4+C\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      }
